Key code changes

internal/external/errors.go — Added ErrorClass and ClassifyError as the single bounded classification API; added RetryExhaustedError; preserved underlying causes; ErrNotFound is permanent.

internal/external/observability.go — Uses ClassifyError for Prometheus labels and structured logs; retry exhaustion is reported separately.

internal/external/retry.go — Returns RetryExhaustedError when the configured retry budget is consumed while preserving the original retryable cause.

internal/external/reddit/worker.go — Uses the shared exported ClassifyError API in worker failure logs.

internal/external/testutil/scripted_client.go — New deterministic HTTP failure-injection harness with ordered outcomes and fallback to a real base HTTP client.

internal/external/testutil/scripted_client_test.go — Tests ordered scripted responses, base fallback, and injected transport errors.

internal/integration/reddit_worker_recovery_test.go — Exercises real Reddit worker scheduling through source outage and restoration; confirms the worker continues and then shuts down cleanly.

internal/integration/resilience_integration_test.go — Adds integration coverage for retry exhaustion and fail-closed expired cache behavior.

scripts/verify-sprint16.ps1 — Repeatable Sprint 16 verification gate: Go version, gofmt, unit tests, race tests, go vet, and targeted resilience integration tests.

Resilience behavior

Retry exhaustion: errors.Is(err, ErrRetryExhausted) is true while the original ErrUpstream/ErrTimeout/ErrRateLimited cause remains discoverable with errors.Is/errors.As.

Stale data: expired cache entries become misses; the application fetches fresh data and does not silently return stale entries when the dependency is unavailable.

Worker recovery: a failed scheduled run is isolated; the scheduler continues and subsequent runs can succeed once the dependency recovers.

Startup: PostgreSQL remains a hard dependency. Reddit is a recoverable worker dependency and is validated when workers are enabled.